{"type": "answer", "t": "2026-11-16T13:54:46-05:00", "question_id": "q1794854881", "question": "Does waste_offset apply to each new pass, not just the game's first draw?", "game": "K473-20261116-130408-632c", "n": 18, "text": "As a general rule, yes. Whenever the last card in the waste pile is the only available play. The \"rule\" is enforced less and less as the stock is depleted (and \"known\" cards become more obvious). At some point, it becomes a \"gut feel\" decision (which is not something I can easily define, but hope my studies may be able to better inform as we go, for example, by knowing how many stock turns remain as a determinant in making that decision). Some decisions may ultimately have to remain as \"gut feel,\" but one of my goals is to minimize those decisions with more informed rules that can still be derived without memorization tricks or card-counting hacks.", "via": "panel"}
