{"type": "move", "n": 27, "move_no": 14, "key": "2Hh", "text": "2♥h", "token": "2HhXCw", "think_ms": 539657, "view": {"stock": 7, "waste": ["5H", "XC", "2H"], "under": 6, "cols": [{"down": 0, "up": ["5S", "4D"]}, {"down": 0, "up": ["7C", "6D", "5C", "4H"]}, {"down": 2, "up": ["8D"]}, {"down": 0, "up": ["2D"]}, {"down": 3, "up": ["JS", "XH"]}, {"down": 5, "up": ["9H", "8C"]}, {"down": 6, "up": ["7H", "6S", "5D", "4S", "3H"]}], "home": ["2S", "AH", null, null]}, "plays": [{"key": "2Hh", "text": "2♥h"}, {"key": "7Cc", "text": "7♣c"}, {"key": "7Hf", "text": "7♥f"}, {"key": "2Sg", "text": "2♠g"}, {"key": "s", "text": "s"}], "choices": 5, "note": "7♥f and 2♥h are functionally equivalent at this moment since the unblocked X♣ on the waste pile won't change the decision to subsequently make the 7♥f tableau play. That said, I find that making the automatic plays as soon as they're available helps me to see the next potential waste-card play (X♣ in this case) more directly, reducing my likelihood of not seeing a \"better\" subsequent play than the one currently being considered.", "t": "2026-11-16T14:12:14-05:00"}
{"type": "move", "n": 28, "move_no": 15, "key": "7Hf", "text": "7♥f", "token": "7Hf9Dg", "think_ms": 180910, "view": {"stock": 7, "waste": ["JD", "5H", "XC"], "under": 5, "cols": [{"down": 0, "up": ["5S", "4D"]}, {"down": 0, "up": ["7C", "6D", "5C", "4H"]}, {"down": 2, "up": ["8D"]}, {"down": 0, "up": ["2D"]}, {"down": 3, "up": ["JS", "XH"]}, {"down": 5, "up": ["9H", "8C"]}, {"down": 6, "up": ["7H", "6S", "5D", "4S", "3H"]}], "home": ["2S", "2H", null, null]}, "plays": [{"key": "7Cc", "text": "7♣c"}, {"key": "7Hf", "text": "7♥f"}, {"key": "3Hh", "text": "3♥h"}, {"key": "2Sg", "text": "2♠g"}, {"key": "s", "text": "s"}], "choices": 5, "note": "No 3♥h play since 2♣ still needs a place to play, so 7♥f seems to be the best available play.", "revealed": "9D", "t": "2026-11-16T14:15:15-05:00"}
{"type": "note", "after": 28, "text": "COMMENT: I'm very aware of the 3♥h-4♥h sequence, which may be played at some point to keep the game \"moving\" (not necessarily progressing). With the 4♦ available to take a black 3, that may come in handy, but generally speaking, as long as I have a higher-rank card to play that will open a column for a king (in the current case, 7♣c), I won't \"clog\" the 4♦ with 3♣ and 2♦ at this point. I would put that move off as much as possible, hoping for the A♣ and 2♣ to get played first.", "t": "2026-11-16T14:23:05-05:00"}
{"type": "note", "after": 28, "text": "COMMENT: Two additional overarching faucets of my game-play strategy are \"Kings out\" and \"Foundation set.\" Two things that seem intuitively progressive as general principles are to get all of the kings out as soon as possible and all of the aces on the foundation as soon as possible. These two cases seem to afford the most flexibility and play availability since it allows me to have more options with the middle cards of a run (being played down-rank on kings or up-rank on the foundation). Both of these seem to lead to more potential for cards in the remaining (unopen) columns to be revealed, and therefore, played.", "t": "2026-11-16T14:32:51-05:00"}
