{"type": "move", "n": 30, "move_no": 16, "key": "3Ca", "text": "3♣a", "token": "3Ca2Cw", "think_ms": 414380, "view": {"stock": 4, "waste": ["KD", "2C", "3C"], "under": 8, "cols": [{"down": 0, "up": ["5S", "4D"]}, {"down": 0, "up": ["7C", "6D", "5C", "4H"]}, {"down": 2, "up": ["8D"]}, {"down": 0, "up": ["2D"]}, {"down": 3, "up": ["JS", "XH"]}, {"down": 5, "up": ["9H", "8C", "7H", "6S", "5D", "4S", "3H"]}, {"down": 5, "up": ["9D"]}], "home": ["2S", "2H", null, null]}, "plays": [{"key": "3Ca", "text": "3♣a"}, {"key": "3Cb", "text": "3♣b"}, {"key": "7Cc", "text": "7♣c"}, {"key": "8Cg", "text": "8♣g"}, {"key": "3Hh", "text": "3♥h"}, {"key": "2Sf", "text": "2♠f"}, {"key": "s", "text": "s"}], "choices": 7, "note": "3♣a and 3♣b are functionally equivalent. Leaving the 4♥ open for the possible 3♥h+4♥h run give 3♣a a minor psychological edge (not knowing what's coming, but still hopefully that the A♣ will be playable soon. But that's getting into hope and speculative \"gut_feel\" level of play to a small and less-impactful way, especially with the 2♣ being revealed on the heals of 3♣a.", "t": "2026-11-16T14:41:27-05:00"}
{"type": "answer", "t": "2026-11-16T14:48:53-05:00", "question_id": "q1794858098", "question": "At #28 you'd avoid clogging 4♦ with 3♣. What changed here?", "game": "K473-20261116-130408-632c", "n": 30, "text": "Hoping for A♣ soon, so 3♥+4♥ can be played after my next play, which will be 2♣f. You can call it intuitive hope/foresight. If not playing 3♣b works out, I won't have to waste a move of to eventually play 3♣a before 3♥h+4♥h. Again, a lot of it is gut-feel because I don't have \"perfect knowledge\" of the stock pile, and I have zero-knowledge of face-down tableau cards.", "via": "panel"}
